{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory handled the high-acuity ICU context well: it repeatedly emphasized that seizure cessation did not mean safety, gave actionable red flags, maintained NPO/medication boundaries, and built a staged-result follow-up plan. It also completed several high-order behaviors, including reprioritizing toward EEG/ongoing coma risks, verifying ambiguous EEG/medication information, and helping the family navigate ICU communication. However, the workspace disclosed a right internal jugular deep venous catheter, and the doctor did not give the required family-facing line/tube safety boundaries or line complication warning signs. That is a minor responsibility-chain omission under RC6, which caps the grade at 2 despite the many strengths.",
